    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97) and **Trea Turner** (76.36). **Yordan Alvarez** provides our highest efficiency score of the day, buoyed by an elite 0.448 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Montero. Meanwhile, **Trea Turner** remains our primary engine for the scarce stolen base category; despite Thornton\u2019s moderate xERA, the matchup sets up perfectly for **Trea Turner** to exploit the opposition's catcher efficiency, earning a top-tier score thanks to his leadoff spot and a 19% boost from the pitcher\u2019s projected weakness. Joining this high-floor cohort, **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Kyle Schwarber** (75.51) offer strong platoon-advantage profiles that prioritize high-volume production in their respective spots in the lineup.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card involved the utility slot and the final bench position. **Carson Benge** (45.02) was the closest exclusion, falling just short of the efficiency required to usurp the likes of **Lars Nootbaar** or **Kazuma Okamoto**. While **Carson Benge** benefited from a leadoff assignment, the aggressive optimization against Wheeler forced him to the bench in favor of more favorable matchups. We are also monitoring **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (60.10) closely; while his score is strong, he faces the most dangerous arm of our starters in Misiorowski (2.74 xERA). Owners should note the inherent risk there, as the matchup efficiency for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is almost entirely driven by his lineup positioning and dynamic platoon advantage rather than a soft pitching matchup. We have opted to keep **Hyeseong Kim** and **Gary Sanchez** on the sidelines as they remain unavailable for selection, ensuring we maximize our daily caps with active, high-projection contributors.",
